{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"set -euo pipefail\nprintf '%s\\\\n' '--- context.json ---'\ncat /Users/chrgre01/src/Sapi/verification/example_site/spaces/graphics/outputs/space_overview/subspace--graphics/context.json\nprintf '%s\\\\n' '--- records files ---'\nfind /Users/chrgre01/src/Sapi/verification/example_site/spaces/graphics/sources/records -maxdepth 1 -type f | sort\nprintf '%s\\\\n' '--- claims files ---'\nfind /Users/chrgre01/src/Sapi/verification/example_site/spaces/graphics/claims -maxdepth 1 -type f | sort\nprintf '%s\\\\n' '--- relations files ---'\nfind /Users/chrgre01/src/Sapi/verification/example_site/spaces/graphics/relations -maxdepth 1 -type f | sort\nprintf '%s\\\\n' '--- topics files ---'\nfind /Users/chrgre01/src/Sapi/verification/example_site/spaces/graphics/topics -maxdepth 1 -type f | sort\"","aggregated_output":"--- context.json ---\n{\n  \"claims\": [\n    {\n      \"added_at\": \"2026-04-26T16:44:00Z\",\n      \"claim_id\": \"claim-a-regular-grid-of-environment-tiles-can-support-both-collision-behavior-and-shad--202b441327e8\",\n      \"evidence_excerpts\": [\n        \"To control the virtual humans\\u2019 motion, we subdivided the floor of the environment into regular-sized tiles.\",\n        \"Several types of information can be stored, but presently, we only use this information for collision detection and shadowing.\"\n      ],\n      \"schema_version\": \"claim_record_v1\",\n      \"short_title\": \"Grid tiles guide motion\",\n      \"source_id\": \"source-02-image-based-crowd-rendering--565ae2b0e3a1\",\n      \"text\": \"A regular grid of environment tiles can support both collision behavior and shadowing decisions for moving virtual humans.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"added_at\": \"2026-04-26T16:36:26Z\",\n      \"claim_id\": \"claim-a-shader-is-a-gpu-directed-program-that-describes-rendering-processes-for-turnin--64c2250afac1\",\n      \"evidence_excerpts\": [\n        \"Le shadercoding d\\u00e9signe l'action de coder un shader. Celui-ci est un programme s'adressant directement \\u00e0 la carte graphique, aussi appel\\u00e9 GPU pour Graphic Processing Unit, de l'ordinateur sur lequel il est ex\\u00e9cut\\u00e9. Il d\\u00e9crit chaque \\u00e9tape du rendu, c'est-\\u00e0-dire chaque processus qui vont permettre \\u00e0 la machine d'afficher une image en fonction des informations des points dans l'espace 3D et de leurs propri\\u00e9t\\u00e9s physiques.\"\n      ],\n      \"schema_version\": \"claim_record_v1\",\n      \"short_title\": \"Shaders direct GPU rendering\",\n      \"source_id\": \"source-01-sphere-tracing-a-geometric-method-for-the-antialiased-ray-tracing-of-implicit-surfaces--eee351440d34\",\n      \"text\": \"A shader is a GPU-directed program that describes rendering processes for turning 3D spatial data and physical properties into an image.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"added_at\": \"2026-04-26T17:15:35Z\",\n      \"claim_id\": \"claim-a-two-pass-accumulation-field-method-fits-directly-into-the-opengl-pipeline-and--bf684a8c9b90\",\n      \"evidence_excerpts\": [\n        \"Therefore we propose the Seed Point Method, a technique that uses two render-passes: one to merge the nodes in their pixel-sized bins and one to create the actual density field. In the first pass the node coordinates xi are mapped to pixel positions xi' of an Accumulation Field. The Accumulation Field is a frame buffer object (FBO) in screen resolution.\"\n      ],\n      \"schema_version\": \"claim_record_v1\",\n      \"short_title\": \"Two passes avoid hierarchies\",\n      \"source_id\": \"source-05-interactive-level-of-detail-rendering-of-large-graphs--df4eb719b5f7\",\n      \"text\": \"A two-pass accumulation-field method fits directly into the OpenGL pipeline and avoids extra point-hierarchy storage for node aggregation.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"added_at\": \"2026-04-26T17:05:42Z\",\n      \"claim_id\": \"claim-a-useful-taxonomy-for-foveated-rendering-classifies-methods-by-required-input-da--a46ce25de499\",\n      \"evidence_excerpts\": [\n        \"The proposed taxonomy classifies current foveated rendering methods according to three dimensions: required input data type, foveation principle, and rendering paradigm.\"\n      ],\n      \"schema_version\": \"claim_record_v1\",\n      \"short_title\": \"Taxonomy has three dimensions\",\n      \"source_id\": \"source-04-foveated-rendering-a-state-of-the-art-survey--2a4e30f52f30\",\n      \"text\": \"A useful taxonomy for foveated rendering classifies methods by required input data type, foveation principle, and rendering paradigm.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"added_at\": \"2026-04-26T16:44:00Z\",\n      \"claim_id\": \"claim-alpha-channel-multipass-rendering-can-recolor-significant-body-regions-such-as-c--265615107527\",\n      \"evidence_excerpts\": [\n        \"We performed multipass rendering using the alpha channel to select the parts to render. For each pass, we change the impostor polygon color to the desired color.\",\n        \"Computing a texture modulation preserves the shading because it\\u2019s already included in the texture.\"\n      ],\n      \"schema_version\": \"claim_record_v1\",\n      \"short_title\": \"Multipass coloring diversifies avatars\",\n      \"source_id\": \"source-02-image-based-crowd-rendering--565ae2b0e3a1\",\n      \"text\": \"Alpha-channel multipass rendering can recolor significant body regions such as clothes, hair, and skin to increase avatar variety while preserving baked texture shading.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"added_at\": \"2026-04-26T17:05:42Z\",\n      \"claim_id\": \"claim-complex-vr-scenes-exceed-the-efficient-real-time-rendering-capacity-of-current-d--4b00d0d7a546\",\n      \"evidence_excerpts\": [\n        \"The source states that rendering overhead continues to increase as VR scenes include diverse materials, more dynamic objects, and more complex simulated physical phenomena; it also reports a visual latency tolerance threshold of approximately 13 ms for the human visual system.\"\n      ],\n      \"schema_version\": \"claim_record_v1\",\n      \"short_title\": \"VR latency causes discomfort\",\n      \"source_id\": \"source-04-foveated-rendering-a-state-of-the-art-survey--2a4e30f52f30\",\n      \"text\": \"Complex VR scenes exceed the efficient real-time rendering capacity of current devices, and delayed rendering can make displayed content inconsistent with user interaction, causing discomfort.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"added_at\": \"2026-04-26T16:36:26Z\",\n      \"claim_id\": \"claim-creating-original-shaders-requires-substantial-mathematical-and-technical-fluenc--7ec21177eabc\",\n      \"evidence_excerpts\": [\n        \"Un shader se d\\u00e9crit donc \\u00e0 l'aide de ph\\u00e9nom\\u00e8nes physiques et math\\u00e9matiques parfois complexes, faisant appel aux matrices et leurs transform\\u00e9es, ou encore aux vecteurs et aux diff\\u00e9rentes op\\u00e9rations possibles entre eux. Il faut alors avoir une base de connaissances scientifiques et techniques relativement pouss\\u00e9e, si l'on souhaite coder ses propres shaders.\"\n      ],\n      \"schema_version\": \"claim_record_v1\",\n      \"short_title\": \"Shadercraft requires mathematical fluency\",\n      \"source_id\": \"source-01-sphere-tracing-a-geometric-method-for-the-antialiased-ray-tracing-of-implicit-surfaces--eee351440d34\",\n      \"text\": \"Creating original shaders requires substantial mathematical and technical fluency in functions, vectors, matrices, and spatial reasoning.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"added_at\": \"2026-04-26T16:56:22Z\",\n      \"claim_id\": \"claim-cuda-image-space-distance-transforms-skeletonization-path-computation-and-attrac--46de973cba61\",\n      \"evidence_excerpts\": [\n        \"The CUDA implementation takes about 4 milliseconds for distance, feature transform, and skeletonization on the same image, about 0.8 seconds per iteration for the graph in Figure 7a-b, and is reported as roughly 100 times faster than the CPU-based AFMM.\"\n      ],\n      \"schema_version\": \"claim_record_v1\",\n      \"short_title\": \"CUDA accelerates skeleton bundling\",\n      \"source_id\": \"source-03-skeleton-based-edge-bundling-for-graph-visualization--1a3dfa0e6b4c\",\n      \"text\": \"CUDA image-space distance transforms, skeletonization, path computation, and attraction make the skeleton-based edge bundling pipeline substantially faster than a CPU AFMM implementation on the tested graphs.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"added_at\": \"2026-04-26T16:36:26Z\",\n      \"claim_id\": \"claim-digital-art-practice-must-negotiate-the-tension-between-scientific-technical-pro--0ddadf7f5e3d\",\n      \"evidence_excerpts\": [\n        \"L'artiste num\\u00e9rique veut exprimer une sensation, un v\\u00e9cu, cr\\u00e9er du sensible au travers de machines logiques, r\\u00e9fl\\u00e9chissant \\u00e0 base de 0 et de 1. Une r\\u00e9flexion logique et technique en amont est donc toujours n\\u00e9cessaire pour r\\u00e9aliser une \\u0153uvre num\\u00e9rique.\"\n      ],\n      \"schema_version\": \"claim_record_v1\",\n      \"short_title\": \"Digital art bridges calculation\",\n      \"source_id\": \"source-01-sphere-tracing-a-geometric-method-for-the-antialiased-ray-tracing-of-implicit-surfaces--eee351440d34\",\n      \"text\": \"Digital art practice must negotiate the tension between scientific-technical processes and the desire to produce sensible artistic experience.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"added_at\": \"2026-04-26T17:15:35Z\",\n      \"claim_id\": \"claim-edge-endpoints-can-be-aggregated-by-hill-climbing-on-the-node-density-field-so-t--6e6b82bcec81\",\n      \"evidence_excerpts\": [\n        \"We interpret the node density field as height field and use a hill climbing algorithm to move starting and end points of the edges to the highest point of their visual cluster (the local maximum). The edges whose start points fall into the same cluster and whose end points share another cluster are implicitly aggregated. As result, inner-cluster connections are vanished while inter-cluster connections are emphasized.\"\n      ],\n      \"schema_version\": \"claim_record_v1\",\n      \"short_title\": \"Hill climbing aggregates edges\",\n      \"source_id\": \"source-05-interactive-level-of-detail-rendering-of-large-graphs--df4eb719b5f7\",\n      \"text\": \"Edge endpoints can be aggregated by hill-climbing on the node density field so that inter-cluster connections are emphasized and inner-cluster connections vanish.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"added_at\": \"2026-04-26T17:05:42Z\",\n      \"claim_id\": \"claim-foveated-rendering-can-accelerate-rendering-by-giving-the-foveal-region-high-qua--d710634b4892\",\n      \"evidence_excerpts\": [\n        \"The source explains that foveated rendering performs high-quality rendering in the foveal region and low-quality rendering in the peripheral region, allowing rendering to speed up without sacrificing perceived visual quality.\"\n      ],\n      \"schema_version\": \"claim_record_v1\",\n      \"short_title\": \"Foveation preserves perceived quality\",\n      \"source_id\": \"source-04-foveated-rendering-a-state-of-the-art-survey--2a4e30f52f30\",\n      \"text\": \"Foveated rendering can accelerate rendering by giving the foveal region high quality and the peripheral region lower quality while preserving perceived visual quality.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"added_at\": \"2026-04-26T17:05:42Z\",\n      \"claim_id\": \"claim-foveated-rendering-methods-span-multiple-data-types-foveation-principles-and-ren--0c481572e2ab\",\n      \"evidence_excerpts\": [\n        \"The taxonomy table lists input data types such as image/video, volume data, geometric meshes, point cloud, hologram data, and light field; it also lists foveation principles and rendering paradigms including multi-spatial resolution, LoD, rasterization, ray tracing, ray casting, neural rendering, phase retrieval, and data transmission.\"\n      ],\n      \"schema_version\": \"claim_record_v1\",\n      \"short_title\": \"Foveation spans multiple principles\",\n      \"source_id\": \"source-04-foveated-rendering-a-state-of-the-art-survey--2a4e30f52f30\",\n      \"text\": \"Foveated rendering methods span multiple data types, foveation principles, and rendering paradigms, including image/video, volume data, meshes, point clouds, holograms, light fields, multi-resolution variants, LoD, rasterization, ray tracing, ray casting, neural rendering, phase retrieval, and data transmission.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"added_at\": \"2026-04-26T17:05:42Z\",\n      \"claim_id\": \"claim-foveated-rendering-research-is-organized-around-three-recurring-problems-applyin--aba700066fc3\",\n      \"evidence_excerpts\": [\n        \"The paper identifies three challenges: use the perceptual model of the human visual system to guide foveated rendering, render different regions with different qualities, and integrate foveated rendering into existing rendering paradigms.\"\n      ],\n      \"schema_version\": \"claim_record_v1\",\n      \"short_title\": \"Foveation requires three decisions\",\n      \"source_id\": \"source-04-foveated-rendering-a-state-of-the-art-survey--2a4e30f52f30\",\n      \"text\": \"Foveated rendering research is organized around three recurring problems: applying human-visual-system perceptual models, rendering regions at different qualities, and integrating foveation into rendering paradigms.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"added_at\": \"2026-04-26T16:36:26Z\",\n      \"claim_id\": \"claim-fragment-shaders-map-two-dimensional-pixel-positions-to-colors-and-can-generate--ff479c9f654e\",\n      \"evidence_excerpts\": [\n        \"Pour r\\u00e9sumer, celui-ci va prendre en entr\\u00e9e la position d'un \\u00ab point num\\u00e9rique \\u00bb de l'espace 2D, appel\\u00e9 pixel, et va retourner une couleur pour le pixel correspondant. ... Mais la propri\\u00e9t\\u00e9 premi\\u00e8re du fragment shader peut aussi permettre de g\\u00e9n\\u00e9rer, \\u00e0 l'aide de formules math\\u00e9matiques, des motifs ou patterns particuliers. Ceux-ci peuvent \\u00eatre anim\\u00e9s avec des variables \\u00e9voluant dans le temps ou selon d'autres informations externes.\"\n      ],\n      \"schema_version\": \"claim_record_v1\",\n      \"short_title\": \"Fragment shaders generate patterns\",\n      \"source_id\": \"source-01-sphere-tracing-a-geometric-method-for-the-antialiased-ray-tracing-of-implicit-surfaces--eee351440d34\",\n      \"text\": \"Fragment shaders map two-dimensional pixel positions to colors and can generate animated mathematical patterns responsive to time or external inputs.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"added_at\": \"2026-04-26T17:05:42Z\",\n      \"claim_id\": \"claim-future-foveated-rendering-work-needs-broader-use-of-human-visual-features-improv--36729372977e\",\n      \"evidence_excerpts\": [\n        \"The discussion identifies opportunities in visual masking and other HVS features, computer vision and AI for gaze prediction and reconstruction, hologram and light-field methods, special-effects rendering beyond straightforward ray tracing, objective metrics and datasets, AR fusion, and task uses such as redirected walking.\"\n      ],\n      \"schema_version\": \"claim_record_v1\",\n      \"short_title\": \"Open problems remain broad\",\n      \"source_id\": \"source-04-foveated-rendering-a-state-of-the-art-survey--2a4e30f52f30\",\n      \"text\": \"Future foveated-rendering work needs broader use of human visual features, improved gaze and AI techniques, better methods for new data types, more suitable rendering paradigms, stronger objective quality metrics, and deeper AR and task-oriented applications.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"added_at\": \"2026-04-26T16:56:22Z\",\n      \"claim_id\": \"claim-hierarchical-agglomerative-clustering-with-full-linkage-and-euclidean-distances--759b1a2656e8\",\n      \"evidence_excerpts\": [\n        \"The edge distance is defined over uniformly spaced samples along the edges, d(e_i,e_j)=sqrt(sum_k ||e_ik-e_jk||^2), with N in [50,100], and the authors report that full-linkage HBA gives the best results.\"\n      ],\n      \"schema_version\": \"claim_record_v1\",\n      \"short_title\": \"Sampling clusters similar edges\",\n      \"source_id\": \"source-03-skeleton-based-edge-bundling-for-graph-visualization--1a3dfa0e6b4c\",\n      \"text\": \"Hierarchical agglomerative clustering with full linkage and Euclidean distances between uniformly sampled edge points yields clusters of geometrically close edges that follow graph structure.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"added_at\": \"2026-04-26T16:44:00Z\",\n      \"claim_id\": \"claim-image-based-impostor-rendering-with-positional-and-directional-discretization-ca--3b5de902e034\",\n      \"evidence_excerpts\": [\n        \"To display many different individual people at interactive frame rates, we combined texture compression with multipass rendering.\",\n        \"Our system allows real-time rendering of densely populated large-scale environments. The rendering speed is independent of the avatar model\\u2019s complexity.\"\n      ],\n      \"schema_version\": \"claim_record_v1\",\n      \"short_title\": \"Impostors enable real-time crowds\",\n      \"source_id\": \"source-02-image-based-crowd-rendering--565ae2b0e3a1\",\n      \"text\": \"Image-based impostor rendering with positional and directional discretization can display dense animated crowds in large virtual urban environments at interactive rates.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"added_at\": \"2026-04-26T16:36:26Z\",\n      \"claim_id\": \"claim-mastered-shadercoding-can-support-real-time-artistic-improvisation-that-fuses-co--51c4a707f8d0\",\n      \"evidence_excerpts\": [\n        \"Tout cela \\u00e9tait possible aussi car j'avais de la marge pour improviser et \\u00eatre impulsive du fait de ma ma\\u00eetrise du langage et de la technicit\\u00e9 de cette programmation. J'avais trouv\\u00e9 le moyen technique me correspondant et me permettant de \\u00ab faire na\\u00eetre une \\u0153uvre \\u00bb, par la communion entre le code (la technique), l'image et l'\\u00e9change.\"\n      ],\n      \"schema_version\": \"claim_record_v1\",\n      \"short_title\": \"Mastery enables live improvisation\",\n      \"source_id\": \"source-01-sphere-tracing-a-geometric-method-for-the-antialiased-ray-tracing-of-implicit-surfaces--eee351440d34\",\n      \"text\": \"Mastered shadercoding can support real-time artistic improvisation that fuses code, image, performer, and audience into a live digital performance.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"added_at\": \"2026-04-26T16:36:26Z\",\n      \"claim_id\": \"claim-mathematical-and-technical-constraints-in-shadercoding-can-become-creative-motor--5b703448e7f5\",\n      \"evidence_excerpts\": [\n        \"Ces propos d'Alain nous montre une autre voie de la pratique de l'art num\\u00e9rique : les contraintes peuvent \\u00eatre cr\\u00e9atrices. Ce qui nous est impos\\u00e9 peut nous diriger dans notre cr\\u00e9ativit\\u00e9. La technicit\\u00e9 derri\\u00e8re le shadercoding peut donc \\u00eatre cr\\u00e9atrice, elle peut \\u00eatre un moteur de celle-ci.\"\n      ],\n      \"schema_version\": \"claim_record_v1\",\n      \"short_title\": \"Constraints drive shader creativity\",\n      \"source_id\": \"source-01-sphere-tracing-a-geometric-method-for-the-antialiased-ray-tracing-of-implicit-surfaces--eee351440d34\",\n      \"text\": \"Mathematical and technical constraints in shadercoding can become creative motors rather than merely limiting conditions.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"added_at\": \"2026-04-26T17:15:35Z\",\n      \"claim_id\": \"claim-measured-overview-rendering-stayed-below-one-second-for-several-datasets-up-to-a--d5763f10ba50\",\n      \"evidence_excerpts\": [\n        \"Table 1 reports overview GPU times at 1500x750 resolution: Wiki-Vote with 103,660 edges took 0.3s at 32px and 0.4s at 128px; net150 with 1,538,840 edges took 0.4s at both kernel sizes; the 4.5M dataset with 4,551,564 edges took 1.2s at both kernel sizes.\"\n      ],\n      \"schema_version\": \"claim_record_v1\",\n      \"short_title\": \"Overview rendering stays fast\",\n      \"source_id\": \"source-05-interactive-level-of-detail-rendering-of-large-graphs--df4eb719b5f7\",\n      \"text\": \"Measured overview rendering stayed below one second for several datasets up to about 1.5 million edges, while a 4.55 million-edge dataset required about 1.2 seconds for overview rendering.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"added_at\": \"2026-04-26T16:44:00Z\",\n      \"claim_id\": \"claim-opengl-compressed-textures-and-compact-frame-storage-allow-ten-human-types-with--0cc37130330a\",\n      \"evidence_excerpts\": [\n        \"We then stored the texture using the OpenGL compressed format, which gives a further memory compression ratio of 1:4.\",\n        \"To simulate 10 different types of human with 10 frames of animation each, we need about 25 Mbytes of texture memory.\"\n      ],\n      \"schema_version\": \"claim_record_v1\",\n      \"short_title\": \"Compressed textures enable variety\",\n      \"source_id\": \"source-02-image-based-crowd-rendering--565ae2b0e3a1\",\n      \"text\": \"OpenGL compressed textures and compact frame storage allow ten human types with ten animation frames each to fit in about 25 Mbytes of texture memory.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"added_at\": \"2026-04-26T16:44:00Z\",\n      \"claim_id\": \"claim-packing-each-prerendered-human-sample-into-the-smallest-containing-rectangle-red--c2027548dc18\",\n      \"evidence_excerpts\": [\n        \"Thanks to this process, the resulting new image is much smaller than the original without any loss of image quality.\",\n        \"With our current reorganization strategy, we can reduce the amount of texture memory necessary to store our human images to 25 percent of the original value.\"\n      ],\n      \"schema_version\": \"claim_record_v1\",\n      \"short_title\": \"Sample packing cuts memory\",\n      \"source_id\": \"source-02-image-based-crowd-rendering--565ae2b0e3a1\",\n      \"text\": \"Packing each prerendered human sample into the smallest containing rectangle reduces the texture memory needed for human images to one quarter of the original value without loss of image quality.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"added_at\": \"2026-04-26T16:44:00Z\",\n      \"claim_id\": \"claim-perturbing-an-impostor-plane-toward-a-pca-derived-best-fitting-plane-reduces-vie--e9f84568a82e\",\n      \"evidence_excerpts\": [\n        \"Starting from an impostor plane purely perpendicular to the camera, we \\u201cperturbed\\u201d its orientation using the resulting plane obtained from a PCA of the sample image. This minimized the popping while limiting the introduction of other artifacts.\"\n      ],\n      \"schema_version\": \"claim_record_v1\",\n      \"short_title\": \"PCA planes reduce popping\",\n      \"source_id\": \"source-02-image-based-crowd-rendering--565ae2b0e3a1\",\n      \"text\": \"Perturbing an impostor plane toward a PCA-derived best-fitting plane reduces viewpoint-change popping for walking human impostors while limiting newly introduced distortions.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"added_at\": \"2026-04-26T17:15:35Z\",\n      \"claim_id\": \"claim-pixel-bin-seed-points-reduce-node-density-rendering-work-without-changing-the-de--a2f787a75006\",\n      \"evidence_excerpts\": [\n        \"For large node sets, however, the described method is time inefficient because the amount of textured rectangles depends linearly on the number of nodes within the screen area. Therefore, we extend the method and significantly reduce rendering time by binning nearby node coordinates into pixels. Instead of rasterizing multiple rectangles at the same position, a single weighted rasterization step per bin is then sufficient to create the same density field.\"\n      ],\n      \"schema_version\": \"claim_record_v1\",\n      \"short_title\": \"Seed points preserve density\",\n      \"source_id\": \"source-05-interactive-level-of-detail-rendering-of-large-graphs--df4eb719b5f7\",\n      \"text\": \"Pixel-bin seed points reduce node-density rendering work without changing the density field produced for a given viewport.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"added_at\": \"2026-04-26T16:36:26Z\",\n      \"claim_id\": \"claim-raymarching-can-recreate-three-dimensional-depth-inside-a-fragment-shader-by-mar--eb7e615f4e18\",\n      \"evidence_excerpts\": [\n        \"Une technique permet m\\u00eame de recr\\u00e9er de la profondeur dans le fragment shader et donc d'afficher \\u00e0 nouveau de la 3D : le raymarching. ... Il s'agit de d\\u00e9crire l'espace selon des fonctions de distances en un point donn\\u00e9 ... Ensuite, pour chaque pixel de l'image, on lance un rayon sur lequel on va 'marcher' pas \\u00e0 pas ... rencontrer un objet d\\u00e9crit dans la fonction de distance (appel\\u00e9e commun\\u00e9ment SDF pour Signed Distance Field).\"\n      ],\n      \"schema_version\": \"claim_record_v1\",\n      \"short_title\": \"Raymarching recreates shader depth\",\n      \"source_id\": \"source-01-sphere-tracing-a-geometric-method-for-the-antialiased-ray-tracing-of-implicit-surfaces--eee351440d34\",\n      \"text\": \"Raymarching can recreate three-dimensional depth inside a fragment shader by marching a ray through a distance-field description until it reaches an object.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"added_at\": \"2026-04-26T16:56:22Z\",\n      \"claim_id\": \"claim-repeated-reclustering-with-decreasing-similarity-thresholds-creates-bottom-up-bu--0f90a7b7b684\",\n      \"evidence_excerpts\": [\n        \"The paper starts with a high similarity threshold, decreases delta and reclusters every three to five iterations, producing fewer and larger clusters once earlier iterations have already made edges locally elongated and partially bundled.\"\n      ],\n      \"schema_version\": \"claim_record_v1\",\n      \"short_title\": \"Iterative reclustering coarsens bundles\",\n      \"source_id\": \"source-03-skeleton-based-edge-bundling-for-graph-visualization--1a3dfa0e6b4c\",\n      \"text\": \"Repeated reclustering with decreasing similarity thresholds creates bottom-up bundling in which fine local bundles merge into coarser structures.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"added_at\": \"2026-04-26T16:56:22Z\",\n      \"claim_id\": \"claim-restricting-attraction-to-skeleton-paths-passing-through-endpoint-feature-points--86df6a0326fa\",\n      \"evidence_excerpts\": [\n        \"For each edge, the algorithm selects a skeleton path whose endpoints include the feature points of the edge endpoints; special points whose FT_S(x) lies off that path are mapped by arc-length interpolation onto the path fragment before attraction.\"\n      ],\n      \"schema_version\": \"claim_record_v1\",\n      \"short_title\": \"Path regularization prevents kinks\",\n      \"source_id\": \"source-03-skeleton-based-edge-bundling-for-graph-visualization--1a3dfa0e6b4c\",\n      \"text\": \"Restricting attraction to skeleton paths passing through endpoint feature points prevents sharp kinks caused by feature-transform singularities.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"added_at\": \"2026-04-26T16:36:26Z\",\n      \"claim_id\": \"claim-shader-showdowns-turn-shadercoding-into-a-timed-public-performance-evaluated-thr--a575bceeaf8e\",\n      \"evidence_excerpts\": [\n        \"Plus commun\\u00e9ment appel\\u00e9 Shader Showdown, il s'agit de coder son effet visuel \\u00e0 l'aide d'un shader en 25 ou 30 minutes devant un public. Suite \\u00e0 cette \\u00e9preuve, les participants seront jug\\u00e9s par les spectateurs sur diff\\u00e9rents crit\\u00e8res : l'image finale produite, la technicit\\u00e9 du code mais \\u00e9galement l'\\u00e9volution de l'effet au cours de l'\\u00e9preuve.\"\n      ],\n      \"schema_version\": \"claim_record_v1\",\n      \"short_title\": \"Showdowns stage shader performance\",\n      \"source_id\": \"source-01-sphere-tracing-a-geometric-method-for-the-antialiased-ray-tracing-of-implicit-surfaces--eee351440d34\",\n      \"text\": \"Shader Showdowns turn shadercoding into a timed public performance evaluated through the final image, code technique, and visual evolution during the event.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"added_at\": \"2026-04-26T16:36:26Z\",\n      \"claim_id\": \"claim-shadercoding-blends-programming-mathematics-and-graphics-into-a-digital-art-prac--ba3619b7f801\",\n      \"evidence_excerpts\": [\n        \"Dans un contexte o\\u00f9 l'art num\\u00e9rique est de plus en plus pr\\u00e9sent, il convient de questionner certains de ses aspects, notamment celui du profil de l'artiste technique. Pour se faire, cet article propose une introduction th\\u00e9orique au shadercoding, une discipline m\\u00ealant programmation, math\\u00e9matiques et graphisme, mais \\u00e9galement une r\\u00e9flexion sur la performance d'art num\\u00e9rique au travers de cette pratique, dans des \\u00e9v\\u00e9nements de programmation en temps-r\\u00e9el.\"\n      ],\n      \"schema_version\": \"claim_record_v1\",\n      \"short_title\": \"Shadercoding blends code and art\",\n      \"source_id\": \"source-01-sphere-tracing-a-geometric-method-for-the-antialiased-ray-tracing-of-implicit-surfaces--eee351440d34\",\n      \"text\": \"Shadercoding blends programming, mathematics, and graphics into a digital-art practice that can be theorized technically and performatively.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"added_at\": \"2026-04-26T16:56:22Z\",\n      \"claim_id\": \"claim-skeleton-based-edge-bundling-is-most-appropriate-for-coarse-scale-connectivity-e--14fed4bbcde5\",\n      \"evidence_excerpts\": [\n        \"The limitations section states that any bundling inherently destroys information because edges are overdrawn, cannot be identified separately, and edge directions are distorted, so it should be used for coarse-scale connectivity patterns.\"\n      ],\n      \"schema_version\": \"claim_record_v1\",\n      \"short_title\": \"Bundling trades detail for structure\",\n      \"source_id\": \"source-03-skeleton-based-edge-bundling-for-graph-visualization--1a3dfa0e6b4c\",\n      \"text\": \"Skeleton-based edge bundling is most appropriate for coarse-scale connectivity exploration because bundling overdraws individual edges and distorts edge directions.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"added_at\": \"2026-04-26T16:56:22Z\",\n      \"claim_id\": \"claim-skeletons-of-inflated-edge-cluster-shapes-provide-locally-centered-targets-for-b--27f82ed32127\",\n      \"evidence_excerpts\": [\n        \"The method clusters edges, constructs a thin distance-field shape around each cluster, computes the shape skeleton and skeleton feature transform, then attracts the clustered edges toward that skeleton.\"\n      ],\n      \"schema_version\": \"claim_record_v1\",\n      \"short_title\": \"Skeletons guide edge bundles\",\n      \"source_id\": \"source-03-skeleton-based-edge-bundling-for-graph-visualization--1a3dfa0e6b4c\",\n      \"text\": \"Skeletons of inflated edge-cluster shapes provide locally centered targets for bundling geometrically similar graph edges.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"added_at\": \"2026-04-26T16:56:22Z\",\n      \"claim_id\": \"claim-smoothing-relaxation-and-cushion-shading-let-users-adjust-whether-bundles-appear--f208f3204963\",\n      \"evidence_excerpts\": [\n        \"Smoothing removes the skeleton effect from bundles, relaxation makes bundles thicker with less effect on curvature, and cushion shading modulates saturation and brightness using distance to the skeleton to help users follow overlapping bundles.\"\n      ],\n      \"schema_version\": \"claim_record_v1\",\n      \"short_title\": \"Smoothing controls bundle structure\",\n      \"source_id\": \"source-03-skeleton-based-edge-bundling-for-graph-visualization--1a3dfa0e6b4c\",\n      \"text\": \"Smoothing, relaxation, and cushion shading let users adjust whether bundles appear as sharp organic branches or smoother force-directed-like curves while preserving the computed connectivity pattern.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"added_at\": \"2026-04-26T17:15:35Z\",\n      \"claim_id\": \"claim-straight-line-graph-drawings-can-be-rendered-interactively-with-adjustable-level--d4a598a6ca79\",\n      \"evidence_excerpts\": [\n        \"We propose a technique that allows straight-line graph drawings to be rendered interactively with adjustable level of detail. The approach consists of a novel combination of edge cumulation with density-based node aggregation and is designed to exploit common graphics hardware for speed.\"\n      ],\n      \"schema_version\": \"claim_record_v1\",\n      \"short_title\": \"LOD renders large graphs\",\n      \"source_id\": \"source-05-interactive-level-of-detail-rendering-of-large-graphs--df4eb719b5f7\",\n      \"text\": \"Straight-line graph drawings can be rendered interactively with adjustable level of detail by combining density-based node aggregation with edge cumulation on graphics hardware.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"added_at\": \"2026-04-26T16:56:22Z\",\n      \"claim_id\": \"claim-the-attraction-rule-moves-interior-edge-points-toward-feature-transform-location--8607f298987e\",\n      \"evidence_excerpts\": [\n        \"x_new = [1 - alpha phi(lambda(x)/lambda(e_ei))] x + alpha phi(lambda(x)/lambda(e_ei)) FT_S(x), with phi(t)=[2 min(t,1-t)]^K, so endpoint motion is zero and middle-edge motion is largest.\"\n      ],\n      \"schema_version\": \"claim_record_v1\",\n      \"short_title\": \"Attraction preserves node endpoints\",\n      \"source_id\": \"source-03-skeleton-based-edge-bundling-for-graph-visualization--1a3dfa0e6b4c\",\n      \"text\": \"The attraction rule moves interior edge points toward feature-transform locations on the skeleton while keeping edge endpoints fixed at their node positions.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"added_at\": \"2026-04-26T17:15:35Z\",\n      \"claim_id\": \"claim-the-edge-aggregation-approach-operates-in-image-space-and-does-not-require-preco--da4e8cd6122f\",\n      \"evidence_excerpts\": [\n        \"In contrast to other edge aggregation techniques our technique operates in image space and therefore does not rely on precomputing supporting data structures.\"\n      ],\n      \"schema_version\": \"claim_record_v1\",\n      \"short_title\": \"Image space avoids preprocessing\",\n      \"source_id\": \"source-05-interactive-level-of-detail-rendering-of-large-graphs--df4eb719b5f7\",\n      \"text\": \"The edge aggregation approach operates in image space and does not require precomputed supporting data structures such as hierarchies or meshes.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"added_at\": \"2026-04-26T17:15:35Z\",\n      \"claim_id\": \"claim-the-lago-implementation-supports-interactive-zooming-panning-normalization-contr--0c65d7666097\",\n      \"evidence_excerpts\": [\n        \"LaGO provides zoom and pan operations to support the interactive exploration of visualized graphs. Similar to related density based approaches the bandwidth parameter h is bound to the viewport to support semantic zooming. The user selects a cluster by clicking onto it and the system retrieves the cluster nodes and sorts them according to their degree or a dedicated weight.\"\n      ],\n      \"schema_version\": \"claim_record_v1\",\n      \"short_title\": \"LaGO enables graph exploration\",\n      \"source_id\": \"source-05-interactive-level-of-detail-rendering-of-large-graphs--df4eb719b5f7\",\n      \"text\": \"The LaGO implementation supports interactive zooming, panning, normalization control, color mapping, and detail-on-demand labeling for large graph exploration.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"added_at\": \"2026-04-26T17:15:35Z\",\n      \"claim_id\": \"claim-the-rendering-complexity-remains-linear-in-input-size-with-seed-point-rectangle--8a6cf3a6542e\",\n      \"evidence_excerpts\": [\n        \"The worst case complexity for p pixels, n nodes and m edges is defined as: O(n \\u00b7 Rs + min(n, p) \\u00b7 Rr + m \\u00b7 Re). Thus we are able to maintain a linear dependency towards the size of the input data.\"\n      ],\n      \"schema_version\": \"claim_record_v1\",\n      \"short_title\": \"Complexity stays linear\",\n      \"source_id\": \"source-05-interactive-level-of-detail-rendering-of-large-graphs--df4eb719b5f7\",\n      \"text\": \"The rendering complexity remains linear in input size, with seed-point rectangle work bounded by the smaller of node count and pixel count.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"added_at\": \"2026-04-26T16:44:00Z\",\n      \"claim_id\": \"claim-the-same-image-database-used-for-impostors-can-project-posture-consistent-human--625367fc5d02\",\n      \"evidence_excerpts\": [\n        \"Using the impostor approach, we can also compute and display the moving humans\\u2019 shadows.\",\n        \"With the cost of only one additional polygon corresponding to the projection of the impostor polygon on the ground, we create a shadow corresponding to the human posture.\"\n      ],\n      \"schema_version\": \"claim_record_v1\",\n      \"short_title\": \"Impostors project human shadows\",\n      \"source_id\": \"source-02-image-based-crowd-rendering--565ae2b0e3a1\",\n      \"text\": \"The same image database used for impostors can project posture-consistent human shadows onto the ground at the cost of one additional polygon.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"added_at\": \"2026-04-26T17:05:42Z\",\n      \"claim_id\": \"claim-the-survey-classifies-90-published-foveated-rendering-reports-from-1990-to-2021--d0734ae4812f\",\n      \"evidence_excerpts\": [\n        \"Table 3 is introduced as a summary of 90 published reports on foveated rendering methods from 1990 to 2021, classified according to data type, foveation principle, and rendering paradigm.\"\n      ],\n      \"schema_version\": \"claim_record_v1\",\n      \"short_title\": \"Ninety reports fit taxonomy\",\n      \"source_id\": \"source-04-foveated-rendering-a-state-of-the-art-survey--2a4e30f52f30\",\n      \"text\": \"The survey classifies 90 published foveated-rendering reports from 1990 to 2021 using the three-dimensional taxonomy.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"added_at\": \"2026-04-26T16:44:00Z\",\n      \"claim_id\": \"claim-the-tested-system-renders-10-000-different-humans-in-a-41-260-polygon-village-at--6845dedcbaed\",\n      \"evidence_excerpts\": [\n        \"These humans move in a village modeled with 41,260 polygons. The display updates between 12 and 20 frames per second, depending on the displayed polygonal complexity.\",\n        \"The frame per second rate for 0 people was 26.20; for 1,000 people, it was 24.08; for 5,000 people, it was 18.26; and for 10,000 people, it was 13.35.\"\n      ],\n      \"schema_version\": \"claim_record_v1\",\n      \"short_title\": \"Ten thousand humans remain interactive\",\n      \"source_id\": \"source-02-image-based-crowd-rendering--565ae2b0e3a1\",\n      \"text\": \"The tested system renders 10,000 different humans in a 41,260-polygon village at 12 to 20 frames per second, with measured frame rates falling from 26.20 fps at zero people to 13.35 fps at 10,000 people.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"added_at\": \"2026-04-26T17:15:35Z\",\n      \"claim_id\": \"claim-the-visualization-examples-reveal-interpretable-patterns-in-real-graph-datasets--6f7b292bd09e\",\n      \"evidence_excerpts\": [\n        \"The prominent flight hubs (Atlanta, Chicago, LA, San Francisco, East coast) appear immediately and strong connections like LA \\u21d4 San Francisco are marked by color and width. Figure 10 describes 545,882 weighted edges for county-to-county migration flow, and Figure 13 visualizes 37.6 million OpenStreetMap building nodes with interactive exploration.\"\n      ],\n      \"schema_version\": \"claim_record_v1\",\n      \"short_title\": \"Examples reveal graph patterns\",\n      \"source_id\": \"source-05-interactive-level-of-detail-rendering-of-large-graphs--df4eb719b5f7\",\n      \"text\": \"The visualization examples reveal interpretable patterns in real graph datasets, including flight hubs, migration flows, Net50 structures, and OpenStreetMap building-density patterns.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"added_at\": \"2026-04-26T17:05:42Z\",\n      \"claim_id\": \"claim-visual-acuity-models-and-contrast-sensitivity-models-are-the-two-representative--544eac975fd9\",\n      \"evidence_excerpts\": [\n        \"The survey names visual acuity and contrast sensitivity as the two most representative perceptual models related to foveated rendering and describes fall-off, binocular horopter, ocular dominance, and several contrast sensitivity functions.\"\n      ],\n      \"schema_version\": \"claim_record_v1\",\n      \"short_title\": \"HVS models guide foveation\",\n      \"source_id\": \"source-04-foveated-rendering-a-state-of-the-art-survey--2a4e30f52f30\",\n      \"text\": \"Visual acuity models and contrast sensitivity models are the two representative perceptual-model families used to guide foveated rendering quality allocation.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"freshness\": {\n    \"claim_count\": 42,\n    \"generated_at\": \"2026-04-26T18:20:02Z\",\n    \"input_signature\": \"sha256:4ed1f908168ddb9e1658a9b64fcf4f3d7acc33ab1cdc1408e0d2cc6058cbc0b7\",\n    \"relation_count\": 24,\n    \"source_record_count\": 5,\n    \"topic_count\": 14\n  },\n  \"metadata\": {\n    \"overview_id\": \"subspace--graphics\",\n    \"parent_space_name\": \"computer-science\",\n    \"scope_kind\": \"subspace\",\n    \"scope_name\": \"graphics\",\n    \"scope_title\": \"Graphics\",\n    \"space_name\": \"graphics\"\n  },\n  \"relations\": [\n    {\n      \"below_040_streak\": 0,\n      \"contradiction_confidence_band\": \"unknown\",\n      \"dst_claim_id\": \"claim-foveated-rendering-research-is-organized-around-three-recurring-problems-applyin--aba700066fc3\",\n      \"dst_claim_ref\": \"2\",\n      \"last_evaluated_run_id\": null,\n      \"rationale\": \"The three-dimensional taxonomy elaborates the survey's three design problems into classifiable method dimensions.\",\n      \"relation_file_id\": \"rel-44f0411fc9da42004e