{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"set -euo pipefail\ncontext=/Users/chrgre01/src/Sapi/verification/example_site/spaces/graphics/outputs/space_overview/subspace--graphics/context.json\nprintf '%s\\\\n' '--- top keys/counts ---'\njq '{keys: keys, counts: {claims: (.claims|length), sources: (.source_records|length // .sources|length // 0), relations: (.relations|length), topics: (.topics|length)}}' \\\"\"'$context\"\nprintf '\"'%s\\\\n' '--- sources ---'\njq -r '(.source_records // .sources // [])[] | {source_id, title, abstract, authors, year, source_type, canonical_path, summary}' \\\"\"'$context\"\nprintf '\"'%s\\\\n' '--- topics ---'\njq -r '.topics[] | {topic_id, title, summary, claim_ids, source_ids}' \\\"\"'$context\"\nprintf '\"'%s\\\\n' '--- claims compact ---'\njq -r '.claims[] | {claim_id, short_title, source_id, text}' \\\"\"'$context\"\nprintf '\"'%s\\\\n' '--- relations compact ---'\njq -r '.relations[] | {relation_id, subject_claim_id, object_claim_id, predicate, relation_type, description}' \\\"\"'$context\"'","aggregated_output":"--- top keys/counts ---\n{\n  \"keys\": [\n    \"claims\",\n    \"freshness\",\n    \"metadata\",\n    \"relations\",\n    \"schema_version\",\n    \"source_records\",\n    \"topics\",\n    \"warnings\"\n  ],\n  \"counts\": {\n    \"claims\": 42,\n    \"sources\": 5,\n    \"relations\": 24,\n    \"topics\": 14\n  }\n}\n--- sources ---\n{\n  \"source_id\": \"source-01-sphere-tracing-a-geometric-method-for-the-antialiased-ray-tracing-of-implicit-surfaces--eee351440d34\",\n  \"title\": \"01-sphere-tracing-a-geometric-method-for-the-antialiased-ray-tracing-of-implicit-surfaces\",\n  \"abstract\": null,\n  \"authors\": [\n    \"Florine Fouquart\",\n    \"Chu-Yin Chen\"\n  ],\n  \"year\": null,\n  \"source_type\": \"file\",\n  \"canonical_path\": null,\n  \"summary\": \"Fouquart and Chen frame shadercoding as a digital-art practice where mathematical image generation, GPU rendering technique, and live coding performance converge. The source introduces shader mechanics, emphasizes raymarching and fragment shaders, and argues from practice that technical constraints and mastery can enable real-time artistic improvisation.\"\n}\n{\n  \"source_id\": \"source-02-image-based-crowd-rendering--565ae2b0e3a1\",\n  \"title\": \"02-image-based-crowd-rendering\",\n  \"abstract\": null,\n  \"authors\": [\n    \"Franco Tecchia\",\n    \"Céline Loscos\",\n    \"Yiorgos Chrysanthou\"\n  ],\n  \"year\": null,\n  \"source_type\": \"file\",\n  \"canonical_path\": null,\n  \"summary\": \"Tecchia, Loscos, and Chrysanthou describe an image-based crowd-rendering system for virtual cities that replaces distant animated humans with optimized impostors. The pipeline reduces popping through PCA-informed impostor planes, reduces texture memory through packing and compression, adds variation through alpha-guided multipass coloring, and reports interactive rendering of 10,000 humans in a 41,260-polygon village.\"\n}\n{\n  \"source_id\": \"source-03-skeleton-based-edge-bundling-for-graph-visualization--1a3dfa0e6b4c\",\n  \"title\": \"03-skeleton-based-edge-bundling-for-graph-visualization\",\n  \"abstract\": null,\n  \"authors\": [\n    \"Ozan Ersoy\",\n    \"Christophe Hurter\",\n    \"Fernando V Paulovich\",\n    \"Gabriel Cantareira\",\n    \"Alexandru C Telea\"\n  ],\n  \"year\": null,\n  \"source_type\": \"file\",\n  \"canonical_path\": null,\n  \"summary\": \"Skeleton-based edge bundling constructs bundled layouts for general graphs by clustering geometrically similar edges, inflating each cluster into a distance-field shape, extracting that shape's skeleton, and attracting edges toward skeleton paths. The method is implemented with image-space GPU operations and is presented as a fast, controllable way to reveal coarse connectivity structure while accepting the information loss inherent in edge bundling.\"\n}\n{\n  \"source_id\": \"source-04-foveated-rendering-a-state-of-the-art-survey--2a4e30f52f30\",\n  \"title\": \"04-foveated-rendering-a-state-of-the-art-survey\",\n  \"abstract\": null,\n  \"authors\": [\n    \"Lili Wang\",\n    \"Xuehuai Shi\",\n    \"Yi Liu\"\n  ],\n  \"year\": null,\n  \"source_type\": \"file\",\n  \"canonical_path\": null,\n  \"summary\": \"Wang, Shi, and Liu survey foveated rendering as a perceptually grounded acceleration strategy for VR and related display systems. The source frames the field around HVS perceptual models, regional quality variation, and integration into rendering paradigms, then proposes a three-dimensional taxonomy and applies it to 90 reports from 1990 to 2021.\"\n}\n{\n  \"source_id\": \"source-05-interactive-level-of-detail-rendering-of-large-graphs--df4eb719b5f7\",\n  \"title\": \"05-interactive-level-of-detail-rendering-of-large-graphs\",\n  \"abstract\": null,\n  \"authors\": [\n    \"Michael Zinsmaier\",\n    \"Ulrik Brandes\",\n    \"Oliver Deussen\",\n    \"Hendrik Strobelt\"\n  ],\n  \"year\": null,\n  \"source_type\": \"file\",\n  \"canonical_path\": null,\n  \"summary\": \"The source presents an OpenGL-based level-of-detail renderer for large graph drawings. It combines density-based node aggregation, a two-pass seed-point method, and hill-climbed edge endpoint aggregation to produce interactive visual summaries without precomputed graph hierarchies or meshes. Performance evidence includes a formal linear-cost expression and measured rendering times across graph datasets, while application examples show use in air traffic, migration, random, Net50, and OpenStreetMap data.\"\n}\n--- topics ---\n{\n  \"topic_id\": \"topic-fields-and-local-structure-as-visual-guides\",\n  \"title\": \"Fields and local structure as guides for visual aggregation\",\n  \"summary\": null,\n  \"claim_ids\": [\n    \"claim-edge-endpoints-can-be-aggregated-by-hill-climbing-on-the-node-density-field-so-t--6e6b82bcec81\",\n    \"claim-pixel-bin-seed-points-reduce-node-density-rendering-work-without-changing-the-de--a2f787a75006\",\n    \"claim-skeletons-of-inflated-edge-cluster-shapes-provide-locally-centered-targets-for-b--27f82ed32127\",\n    \"claim-the-attraction-rule-moves-interior-edge-points-toward-feature-transform-location--8607f298987e\",\n    \"claim-restricting-attraction-to-skeleton-paths-passing-through-endpoint-feature-points--86df6a0326fa\",\n    \"claim-raymarching-can-recreate-three-dimensional-depth-inside-a-fragment-shader-by-mar--eb7e615f4e18\",\n    \"claim-fragment-shaders-map-two-dimensional-pixel-positions-to-colors-and-can-generate--ff479c9f654e\"\n  ],\n  \"source_ids\": [\n    \"source-05-interactive-level-of-detail-rendering-of-large-graphs--df4eb719b5f7\",\n    \"source-03-skeleton-based-edge-bundling-for-graph-visualization--1a3dfa0e6b4c\",\n    \"source-01-sphere-tracing-a-geometric-method-for-the-antialiased-ray-tracing-of-implicit-surfaces--eee351440d34\"\n  ]\n}\n{\n  \"topic_id\": \"topic-gpu-pipelines-turn-mathematical-structure-into-real-time-images\",\n  \"title\": \"GPU pipelines turn mathematical structure into real-time images\",\n  \"summary\": null,\n  \"claim_ids\": [\n    \"claim-cuda-image-space-distance-transforms-skeletonization-path-computation-and-attrac--46de973cba61\",\n    \"claim-a-shader-is-a-gpu-directed-program-that-describes-rendering-processes-for-turnin--64c2250afac1\",\n    \"claim-creating-original-shaders-requires-substantial-mathematical-and-technical-fluenc--7ec21177eabc\",\n    \"claim-fragment-shaders-map-two-dimensional-pixel-positions-to-colors-and-can-generate--ff479c9f654e\",\n    \"claim-opengl-compressed-textures-and-compact-frame-storage-allow-ten-human-types-with--0cc37130330a\",\n    \"claim-the-tested-system-renders-10-000-different-humans-in-a-41-260-polygon-village-at--6845dedcbaed\"\n  ],\n  \"source_ids\": [\n    \"source-03-skeleton-based-edge-bundling-for-graph-visualization--1a3dfa0e6b4c\",\n    \"source-01-sphere-tracing-a-geometric-method-for-the-antialiased-ray-tracing-of-implicit-surfaces--eee351440d34\",\n    \"source-02-image-based-crowd-rendering--565ae2b0e3a1\"\n  ]\n}\n{\n  \"topic_id\": \"topic-image-space-geometric-abstraction-for-readable-visual-complexity\",\n  \"title\": \"Image-space geometric abstraction for readable visual complexity\",\n  \"summary\": null,\n  \"claim_ids\": [\n    \"claim-skeletons-of-inflated-edge-cluster-shapes-provide-locally-centered-targets-for-b--27f82ed32127\",\n    \"claim-hierarchical-agglomerative-clustering-with-full-linkage-and-euclidean-distances--759b1a2656e8\",\n    \"claim-the-attraction-rule-moves-interior-edge-points-toward-feature-transform-location--8607f298987e\",\n    \"claim-restricting-attraction-to-skeleton-paths-passing-through-endpoint-feature-points--86df6a0326fa\",\n    \"claim-repeated-reclustering-with-decreasing-similarity-thresholds-creates-bottom-up-bu--0f90a7b7b684\",\n    \"claim-skeleton-based-edge-bundling-is-most-appropriate-for-coarse-scale-connectivity-e--14fed4bbcde5\",\n    \"claim-image-based-impostor-rendering-with-positional-and-directional-discretization-ca--3b5de902e034\",\n    \"claim-packing-each-prerendered-human-sample-into-the-smallest-containing-rectangle-red--c2027548dc18\",\n    \"claim-raymarching-can-recreate-three-dimensional-depth-inside-a-fragment-shader-by-mar--eb7e615f4e18\"\n  ],\n  \"source_ids\": [\n    \"source-03-skeleton-based-edge-bundling-for-graph-visualization--1a3dfa0e6b4c\",\n    \"source-02-image-based-crowd-rendering--565ae2b0e3a1\",\n    \"source-01-sphere-tracing-a-geometric-method-for-the-antialiased-ray-tracing-of-implicit-surfaces--eee351440d34\"\n  ]\n}\n{\n  \"topic_id\": \"topic-image-space-gpu-aggregation-for-real-time-scale\",\n  \"title\": \"Image-space GPU aggregation for real-time visual scale\",\n  \"summary\": null,\n  \"claim_ids\": [\n    \"claim-straight-line-graph-drawings-can-be-rendered-interactively-with-adjustable-level--d4a598a6ca79\",\n    \"claim-pixel-bin-seed-points-reduce-node-densit